before:
Complete local C# example; the app does not execute it:
```csharp
using System;
using System.Threading.Tasks;
Task<int> first = FetchAsync(2, 20);
Task<int> second = FetchAsync(5, 1);
int[] results = await Task.WhenAll(first, second);
Console.WriteLine(string.Join(",", results));
static async Task<int> FetchAsync(int value, int delay)
{
    await Task.Delay(delay);
    return value;
}
```

after:
Follow the order of the two tasks passed to WhenAll.

```csharp
using System;
using System.Threading.Tasks;
Task<int> first = FetchAsync(2, 20);
Task<int> second = FetchAsync(5, 1);
int[] results = await Task.WhenAll(first, second);
Console.WriteLine(string.Join(",", results));
static async Task<int> FetchAsync(int value, int delay)
{
    await Task.Delay(delay);
    return value;
}
```
